<title>HUNGARY: USAID EXTENDS LOAN GUARANTEE TO OTP.</title>
<headline>USAID EXTENDS LOAN GUARANTEE TO OTP.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agency for International Development (USAID) and Hungary's OTP Bank signed a guarentee agreement on Friday with the eventual aim of helping Hungarian small- and medium-size entreprenuers.</p>
<p>&quot;We are very proud of that OTP was the first from among central and eastern European countries to join this program of the U.S. government agency,&quot; Sandor Csanyi, OTP Bank's President and CEO, told the signing ceremony.</p>
<p>The USAID's guarantee will be utilised for the allocation of a loan facility worth $6 million.</p>
<p>On the Budapest Stock Exchange OTP shares closed at 2,450 forints, up 10.</p>
<p>-- Emese Bartha, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
